sequenceDiagram
    participant P as pointer/touch (OSK)
    participant DR as KeyboardDriver (ferrokey-core)
    participant ST as KeyboardState
    participant RT as InputRouter (input.rs)
    participant DL as DaemonLink (daemon.rs)
    participant CL as protocol Client
    participant SRV as ferrokeyd serve
    participant DEV as uinput device
    participant APP as focused application

    P->>DR: KeyAction::Down / Tap / Up
    DR->>ST: press(key, now)
    ST-->>DR: Vec<KeyEvent> (Down/Up, injected modifiers)
    DR->>RT: key_down / key_up
    RT->>DL: (Destination::System)
    DL->>CL: KEY_DOWN / KEY_UP frames
    CL->>SRV: AF_UNIX
    SRV->>SRV: authorize (SO_PEERCRED + session scope)
    SRV->>SRV: rate-limit + held-key ledger
    SRV->>DEV: EV_KEY / EV_SYN
    DEV->>APP: Linux input core -> focused window
